# tests/lir_peephole_lane_test.tg — the Slice 5 peephole and the
# allocator's dead-store elimination lane.
#
# The engine lives in tg_compiler/lir.tg: lir_peephole (the shared
# rewrites — self-move elimination, move subsumption via per-block value
# classes, dead flag-set elimination) and lir_peephole_cond_branch (the
# a64 entry, adding the cmp+cond-branch fusion into a LirCondBranch-
# marked LirJump). The emitter-side fallthrough elision (lir_emit_fn's
# next_block rule) and the allocator's dead-store elimination
# (lir_alloc_registers_mode's finalize pass: no spill record for a value
# dead after the call) are pinned by the same lane.
#
# Rows (each returns a mismatch text on failure; the test asserts the
# empty list):
#   P1 self-move elimination + move subsumption (positive and the
#      redefinition negative), with verify_lir green after the rewrite;
#   P2 dead flag-set elimination (a compare shadowed by the next compare,
#      and a trailing compare, are removed; every consumed compare stays);
#   P3 cmp+cond-branch fusion: the marker shape, verify_lir on both the
#      fused and the raw function, and a strictly smaller emitted word
#      count; the shared entry (non-a64 routes) never fuses;
#   P4 fallthrough branch elision: exactly two words fewer on a chain
#      whose targets are physically next, with the block order unchanged;
#   P5 allocator dead-store elimination: a live-across value keeps its
#      store + reload records, a dead-after value's store record is
#      elided, and verify_lir stays green.
#
# Run with the repo root as the working directory:
#   tg test tests/lir_peephole_lane_test.tg

use std::test::assert

use tg_compiler::lir::{lir_peephole_lane_check}

@test
def test_lir_peephole_lane() -> Unit
  let rows = lir_peephole_lane_check()
  assert(rows.len() == 0, "lir peephole lane mismatches: " + rows.join("; "))
end
